WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.135
-Well, it's Thanksgiving,
so you know what that means.

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:06.338
America's crazy
uncle Mike Lindell is
at the dinner table,

00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:08.574
screaming at the top
of his lungs about voter fraud,

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:10.477
while everyone else
silently ignores him

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.578
and tucks into their
green bean casserole.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.682
Oh, and also, President Biden
tried to talk to a turkey.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.884
[ Laughter ]
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:22.855
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.557
If you did have
some turkey today,

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.759
it almost certainly wasn't one
of these guys

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.596
because they were both pardoned
by President Biden on Monday.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:32.965
And Biden could not help
indulge in some, let's say,

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:35.135
overcooked Thanksgiving puns.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:37.036
-First of all, the votes are in.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:39.873
They've been counted
and verified.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.040
There's no ballot stuffing.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.343
There's no fowl play.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.745
[ Laughter ]
The only red wave this season
is going to be

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.113
a German Shepherd,
Commander,

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.282
who knocks over the cranberry
sauce on our table.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.050
[ Laughter ]
Interesting fact --

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.486
every one of those puns came
from a book called...

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:59.926 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.394
I do forgive him
because he's a grandpa.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:04.397
He's President Grandpa
and he's been a grandpa so long,

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.731
his granddaughter
just got married,

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:07.600
which means,
if Biden wins a second term,

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.769
there's a chance he could be
President Great-Grandpa,

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:10.970
and that would be the first time

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.772
in American history
that's happened.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:13.973
Or the fifth.
I don't know.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.808
I tried to Google it.
I couldn't figure it out.

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:16.575
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:17.710
I entered in...

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.646
...and Google just said,
"Do you really need to know?"

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:22.548
[ Laughter ]
And I said, "Not really."

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.717
And Google said,
"Just come back when you have
something important.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.485
Do you know how many searches
we do in a day?"

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.287
[ Laughter ]
Point is Biden's jokes were bad,

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:30.156
but I'll happily take
some stale puns

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:33.159
over a long rant about how China
is working with Hugo Chávez

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.160
to smuggle in forged ballots

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.830
or whatever Trump used to talk
about during holidays.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.398
[ As Trump ]
They've treated me
very unkindly,

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:40.767
these crooked Democrats,

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.068
maybe worse than anyone
has ever been treated before,

00:01:43.068 --> 00:01:45.204
and that, of course,
is the true meaning

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:46.572
of Mother's Day.

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:48.240
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.409
Remember when he used
to host the Easter Egg Roll

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:51.344
at the White House and...

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.712
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.547
...the bunny would just stand
next to him

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.015
for what felt like forever,

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.384
while Trump would ramble
to children

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.953
about how he rebuilt
the military or something?

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:02.722
[ Laughter ]
And, for some reason,

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.357
that bunny was always
making a face

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.792
like he just walked in
on his parents having sex.

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:08.761
[ Laughter ]
Which, presumably,

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.963
happens all the time because,
you know, they are bunnies.

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:12.831
"Mom, Dad!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.831 --> 00:02:17.069
No, I'm already sharing my room
with 30 brothers and sisters!"

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:18.404
In fairness to Trump,

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.606
I don't know why
his staff went on Amazon

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:22.442
and specifically chose
the costume called...

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.845
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:29.114
I did enjoy Biden's shout-out
to his dog Commander, though.

00:02:29.114 --> 00:02:31.484
That one doesn't quite seem
like a joke to me.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.752
[ As Biden ]
There's no red wave,

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.821
unless Commander knocks over
the cranberry sauce.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.322
I'm serious, folks,
he might do it.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.057
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.092
That dog is crazy!

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.460
I'm scared to death of him.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.362
[ Laughter ]
Last, Thanksgiving,
he jumped out

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.463
and grabbed the carving knife,
held off the Secret Service

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:45.831
[ Laughter ]
for an hour.

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:48.434
They had to throw a net
over him!

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.336
There's also a decent chance
I fell asleep

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.537
on the Acela and dreamed that.

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:52.505
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.873
No, it happened.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.508
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.510
For the most part, it was
a very traditional ceremony.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.678
Although,
there was one odd moment,

00:02:59.678 --> 00:03:02.315
where Biden asked the providers
of the turkeys

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.916
how many more they had,

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:06.419
made a weird joke
about visiting other countries,

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:09.221
and then asked the turkey
if it wanted to talk.

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:11.191
-How many turkeys you got
down there?

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.058
You're raising?
-circle Range grows

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:15.261
about 9.5 million turkeys
a year.

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.263
-God love you,

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.931
Nine and a half million turkeys.

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:20.099
[ Laughter and oohs ]

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.367
I tell you what.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.569
That's like some of the
countries I've been to.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.137
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:26.339
And the --

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.240
Anyway.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.208
Do you want to talk?

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:31.077
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.545
Yeah.

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:34.113
-Wait.
How?

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.482
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:39.118
How is that like some of the
countries you've been to?

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.586
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:43.689
They had that many people
or they had that many turkeys?

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:46.158
No wonder you tried
to get the turkey

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:48.227
to say something
to change the subject.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:50.029
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.096
[ As Biden ]
Bail me out here, brother.

00:03:51.096 --> 00:03:54.700
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.102
With that said, asking a turkey

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:57.903
if they want to talk
into a microphone is very funny.

00:03:57.903 --> 00:03:59.438
[ Laughter ]
Mostly because it's just fun

00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:01.040
to imagine what a turkey
would say.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.376
Would it be like
an Emmy acceptance speech?

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:05.510
"I just want to thank my family
my friends,

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:06.779
my agent, my manager.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.414
Everybody down at the roost
who believed in me.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.648
And I want to say
to my kids at home,

00:04:09.648 --> 00:04:11.517
Jeremy and Delilah, go to bed!"

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:14.120
[ Laughter ]
Also, it is a nice change
of pace

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.222
that the president is willing
to share the mic.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:19.558
You know Trump would never share
the spotlight with two turkeys,

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:21.861
unless he was posing
for a family photo.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:24.797
[ Turkey gobbling ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.437
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.437 --> 00:04:37.309
They do puff their chests out
like they're turkeys.

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:38.778
But, as you heard
in that first clip,

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:40.913
Biden couldn't help
but take a slight jab

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.148
at the supposed red wave

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:44.683
that never materialized
in this year's midterms.

00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:46.018
Many people,
including Republicans,

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:48.087
are still wondering why
that red wave never happened

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:51.490
and at least one GOP pundit
on Fox News had a theory.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.159
-We have a candidate
quality problem,

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.928
but what we've seen is
a real intensification

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.796 line:0%
of this problem
from top to bottom --

00:04:57.796 --> 00:04:59.799 line:0%
not just Senate candidates,
but House candidates,

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:03.102 line:0%
secretary of state candidates,
and governors, and the like.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.236 line:0%
And it's, you know, what I call

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.538 line:0%
the MyPillowization
of the Republican Party,

00:05:06.538 --> 00:05:07.840 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
is we've attracted

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.609 line:0%
these more cartoon characters
and if somebody speaking

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:13.579 line:0%
at a rally with a president
or a presidential candidate

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.114 line:0%
is best known
as a pillow salesman,

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.582 line:0%
run to high heaven.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:19.385
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, you can run,
but you can't hide

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.254
from Mike Lindell's voice.

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:23.122
It doesn't matter
how far away you are,

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.390
you will still be able
to hear him.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.124
It's like that scene
from "Jurassic Park."

00:05:26.124 --> 00:05:27.426
If, at any point, you see

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.395
the water in your glass
rippling, don't worry.

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.731
It just means Mike Lindell
is speaking somewhere.

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.199
[ Laughter ]
But if Republicans are worried

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.933
about the MyPillowization
of their party,

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:36.903
then they're probably not going
to be thrilled

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.904
to hear the latest news
from Mike Lindell Land.

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:41.573
But, in a way, we are
because here's the thing.

00:05:41.573 --> 00:05:44.009
It's Thanksgiving and just
as important as the turkey

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:45.310
and the stuffing
and the football

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:46.478
are the crazy uncles.

00:05:46.478 --> 00:05:47.880 line:0%
And, just in time
for Thanksgiving,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.316 line:0%
old uncle Mike went on one
of his usual,

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.851 line:0%
obscure right-wing TV shows
that you can only get

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:55.087
with rabbit ears or a ham radio

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:56.922
and claimed he had solid proof
that elections

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:58.924
across the country were stolen
from Republicans.

00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:03.629
-We have cyberevidence
of a 37,000-vote flip

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.999
on the Kari Lake race
on Thursday after the election.

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:10.669 line:0%
We have all the Edison data
that came in, in real time,

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:12.838 line:0%
that came through
on all the races,

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:15.708 line:0%
including Finchem,
Blake Masters.

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:16.976 line:0%
They all won, okay?

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.277 line:0%
They all won.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.979 line:0%
This is like we were watching
from every angle.

00:06:20.979 --> 00:06:22.414 line:0%
You go up to Michigan,

00:06:22.414 --> 00:06:25.217 line:0%
they've completely wiped out
the state of Michigan,

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:26.652 line:0%
stole the legislatures,

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:27.486 line:0%
everything.
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:27.486 --> 00:06:29.922 line:0%
Other races, from Oz.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:31.290 line:0%
Oz really won.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.858 line:0%
There's all these
different races.

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:35.594 line:0%
But they were caught, so.

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:39.298 line:0%
But Arizona is the gateway
to all of our --

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:41.534 line:0%
to expose everything, everybody.

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:44.937
We have to --
We have to get Arizona.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.672
They need to do
a new election.

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:47.739
[ Laughter ]
-That's right,

00:06:47.739 --> 00:06:49.541
they need to do a new election.

00:06:49.541 --> 00:06:51.410
He screams like he's
doing dialogue

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:55.047 line:0%
from a straight-to-DVD knockoff
of "Back to the Future."

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:56.982 line:0%
[ As Lindell ]
Marty, we got to go back in time

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:58.184 line:0%
and do a new election.

00:06:58.184 --> 00:07:00.519
I hooked up the DeLorean
to the clock tower

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:03.489
and got electrocuted
and that's why I talk like this.

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:05.958
[ Laughter ]
Also, I found
that Sports Almanac

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.493
and bet a million dollars on

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:08.694
Da Bears!

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:10.830
[ Laughter ]
Now, you might be wondering why

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.231
we're spending any time
at all talking

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:13.432
about a pillow salesman.

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:14.967
Well, aside from the fact
that it's Thanksgiving

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:16.736
and we're celebrating
the importance of crazy uncles,

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:18.904
Lindell has also been
a major influence

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:20.272
within the election
denial movement.

00:07:20.272 --> 00:07:21.574
As we noted before,

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.675
he's endorsed candidates,
appeared at Trump rallies,

00:07:23.675 --> 00:07:25.511
and, according
to The New York Times,
he spent...

00:07:39.858 --> 00:07:41.794
First of all, I don't believe
he has researchers.

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:43.429
I believe he has guys
who are willing

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:46.665
to say they did research, just
to collect an easy paycheck.

00:07:46.665 --> 00:07:48.300
[ As Lindell ]
Alright, gang, did you guys do

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.102
all the research I asked for?

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:52.204
"Uh, yeah, definitely.

00:07:52.204 --> 00:07:54.206
[ Laughter ]
Um...

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:56.475
we found a bunch
of cyberevidence

00:07:56.475 --> 00:07:59.545
[ Laughter ]
using the, uh, Edison data

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:00.412
to prove that they, uh,

00:08:00.412 --> 00:08:01.847
completely wiped out

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:02.881
the state of Michigan?"

00:08:02.881 --> 00:08:03.949
Sounds good, fellas.

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:05.351
Here's a million dollars.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:08.154
[ Laughter ]
Now, if you ever hear
Lindell yelling,

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:09.955
just grab a lab coat
and go get paid.

00:08:09.955 --> 00:08:11.623
Also, how does
he have this much money?

00:08:11.623 --> 00:08:13.192
His pillows can be that good.
Otherwise,

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:15.828
he wouldn't always look like
he hasn't slept in five years.

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:16.795
[ Laughter ]
But I don't know.

00:08:16.795 --> 00:08:18.063
Maybe they are.
I don't know.

00:08:18.063 --> 00:08:20.098
So, let me try one.
Here we go.

00:08:20.098 --> 00:08:21.700
[ Laughter ]
You know what?
I will say,

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:22.802
doesn't look that bad.

00:08:23.336 --> 00:08:24.537
[ Clang ]

00:08:24.537 --> 00:08:27.406
[ Laughter ]

00:08:30.442 --> 00:08:32.211
[ Applause ]
No. [Indistinct]

00:08:35.081 --> 00:08:36.114
[ Clang ]

00:08:36.114 --> 00:08:39.118
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:42.487 --> 00:08:44.189
[ Fresh laughter and applause ]

00:08:44.189 --> 00:08:46.993
Why did we move our sound
effects guy to Australia?

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:48.961
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:51.797
We're going to get this one.

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:53.765
[ Clang ]

00:08:53.765 --> 00:08:56.202
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:56.202 --> 00:08:57.970
Okay, you guys, I want
to make something clear.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.106
This is not a real MyPillow!

00:09:00.106 --> 00:09:02.107
I do not want to get sued
by Mike Lindell because,

00:09:02.107 --> 00:09:03.976
if I am, I think I would laugh
through the whole trial

00:09:03.976 --> 00:09:06.078
and the jury would turn
against me for being immature.

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:07.947
If you want to sue someone,
sue Sal. He writes these.

00:09:07.947 --> 00:09:09.482
I barely know what any
of these words mean.

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:12.318
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.254 --> 00:09:16.087
[ Clang ]

00:09:16.087 --> 00:09:18.190
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.092
Lindell is also --

00:09:20.092 --> 00:09:21.894
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.894 --> 00:09:24.897
Lindell is also currently banned
from Twitter, as of this taping,

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:26.431
but he's been very public
about the fact

00:09:26.431 --> 00:09:27.533
that he wants his account back.

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:30.068
In fact, he even issued
a direct plea

00:09:30.068 --> 00:09:32.170
to Twitter's new owner,
Elon Musk.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:35.741
-My shout-out to Elon Musk
would be, you know,

00:09:35.741 --> 00:09:40.613
if your site should be a new
platform of free speech,

00:09:40.613 --> 00:09:42.881
but yet, you're going
to carve out the guys that talk

00:09:42.881 --> 00:09:46.619
about our election crimes
and our election integrity,

00:09:46.619 --> 00:09:47.920
I don't think it's
that free, Steve.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.156
I think it's --
I think I would like to do

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:52.258
a shout-out
to Elon Musk right now.

00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:53.992
Hey, check out the evidence.

00:09:53.992 --> 00:09:57.596
I was banned because I was
telling the truth.

00:09:57.596 --> 00:09:59.831
-Would you commit, right now,

00:09:59.831 --> 00:10:03.068
to do an open live Twitter
with Elon Musk

00:10:03.068 --> 00:10:05.571
about what you believe is
the voter fraud related

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:09.408
to machines and other things
in the 2020 election, sir?

00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:10.542
-Absolutely.

00:10:10.542 --> 00:10:12.778
I'd fly to him,
do whatever it takes.

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:15.714
And I would do that any day,
anytime,

00:10:15.714 --> 00:10:17.382
any time of day or night,

00:10:17.382 --> 00:10:20.452
and I'll drop everything I have
to do that.

00:10:20.452 --> 00:10:22.120
-Alright, first of all, dude,
you're on TV.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:23.989
Wear something nicer
than a plaid shirt.

00:10:23.989 --> 00:10:24.924
[ Laughter ]
Second of all...

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:27.325
[ Applause ]

00:10:27.325 --> 00:10:28.060
Seriously.

00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:32.665
Be a professional.

00:10:32.665 --> 00:10:36.368
[ Laughter ]

00:10:36.368 --> 00:10:38.937
Second of all, you don't need
to call it a shout-out.

00:10:38.937 --> 00:10:40.473
Everything you say
is a shout-out.

00:10:40.473 --> 00:10:41.974
[ Laughter ]

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:44.677
Anyway, now that we've had
our fun, let's remember

00:10:44.677 --> 00:10:46.011
that it's Thanksgiving.

00:10:46.011 --> 00:10:47.879
It's a time for us to come
together with our friends,

00:10:47.879 --> 00:10:49.581
our families,
and our communities,

00:10:49.581 --> 00:10:52.384
to spend time with another,
to give thanks,

00:10:52.384 --> 00:10:53.986
and, of course,
to ignore our crazy uncles.

00:10:53.986 --> 00:10:55.687
And, if you have a crazy uncle
at Thanksgiving this year,

00:10:55.687 --> 00:10:57.790
don't worry.
Just remember the first rule --

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:00.292
whatever you do,
do not turn to them and say...

00:11:00.292 --> 00:11:01.460
-Do you want to talk?

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:04.296
[ Laughter ]

00:11:04.296 --> 00:11:05.564
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:05.564 --> 00:11:09.235
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

